# A window is READONLY, so it declares no mutable walk. `iterateMut` lives on
# the owning list, where an exclusive receiver can be had.
#
# The refusal lands at the member, where the name is. The binding is incidental
# now: while the mono stayed lenient this only reported because the result was
# BOUND, and the same call in statement position was dropped in silence.
main: function is {
    ns: (ListVal i64)
    ns.append from: 1
    sl: ns.slice from: 0 to: 1
    it: sl.iterateMut
    print "unreachable"
}
